 "_note": "Shared boundary cases for the kanban request bodies (kanban design 'Request rules'; Requirements 1.2, 1.5, 2.6, 2.7, 3.4, 3.12, 4.7). The Flask schema tests (task 3.6, 5.6) and the frontend kanbanRules tests (task 7.2) both read this file, as auth-field-cases.json and board-field-cases.json are read. Each case starts from its form's base body, applies 'set' then 'drop', and expects one of: 'accepted' (a map of the normalized values the schema must return for the keys it lists; the other base keys keep their base values; the output keys must equal the body's key set), 'fields' (the exact map of field messages), or 'rejected_without_fields' (a 400 with a body-level message and no 'fields', for an empty PATCH body). Values: {\"repeat\": s, \"times\": n} is s repeated n times. Lengths count Unicode code points. Forms: column_create (E13), column_update (E14), column_reorder (E16), card_create (E17), card_update (E18), card_position (E20). A blank or whitespace-only description normalizes to null (L6). expected_position_version accepts integers 0 to 2147483647 and rejects booleans, floats, strings and null. before_column_id and before_card_id must be present and may be null. Messages are fixed strings and never echo a value.",
